a racist display at a henderson shopping  mall shocking many in the community mary  jane bellezza reports on what's causing  the outrage  community leaders filled the galleria  mall parking lot this morning to protest  a racist display that was up for several  weeks stating racism is not welcomed in  our community the national action  network and other civil rights  organizations are outraged the network  is reporting the racist display was  shown in front of families and children  from may 30th to july 5th the display by  las vegas railway society shows a black  man being prepared to be hung robert  bush the local president of the national  action network says the goal of monday's  protest is to show the community that  racism will not be tolerated and they  are demanding an apology not only was it  racist but but there are better ways  to depict black people in their history  of the railways such as blacks were the  first porters  such as blacks built most of the  railways throughout the united states if  they wanted to show history in the  united states then there was a much  better way to be able to do that than  a racist display while the galleria mall  general manager did offer an apology  bush tells me the las vegas railway  society has not yet responded initially  this was reported to the las vegas  action network through email that  display was taken down last week  reporting from sunset and stephanie  street mary jane vallieza live local now  governor sisselok tweeted about the  display today simply stating that racism  has no home in nevada and the display is  completely unacceptable and our  community deserves answers the  galleria's owner brookfield properties  also says it's disgusted by the display
 

